// The `0x` prefix needs one digit of its base (spec/01-lexical.md, Number and
// Int Literals). Without one the longest match is the NUMBER `0` and the name
// `x`, so this line is a name directly after a literal (row suffix-boundary).
// A scanner that takes the prefix greedily reads an Int with no digits.
//
// A static error rejects the program: a non-zero exit status, and nothing
// runs, so nothing prints (spec/README.md, Conformance). The first line
// prints `ran`, so an implementation that finds the error only when it runs
// the program prints `ran` and fails this probe.

print "ran";
print 0x;

// STATIC-ERROR
// STATUS: error
// COVERS: literal suffix-boundary
